# Normalise every text file to LF in the repository, whatever the checkout does
# locally. The rules below predate this and stay because they are the cases that
# actually broke; this catch-all covers the ones that have not yet — Dockerfile,
# .dockerignore, docker-compose.yml and .env.example are all read by tools that
# happen to tolerate CRLF today. Every tracked file is already LF in the index,
# so this changes nothing now (`git ls-files --eol`).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must keep LF endings in the repository. core.autocrlf=true on a
# Windows checkout would otherwise commit CRLF, and bash on the CI runner fails
# on those with "$'\r': command not found" — an error that says nothing about
# the real cause.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The stubbed curl and jq in the publish-cleanup tests are extensionless shell
# scripts, so the rule above does not reach them.
scripts/test-publish-cleanup/stubs/* text eol=lf
